            "value": true
          },
          "font-size": {
            "type": "float",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "CLONER\n\nThis tutorial functions as a template for creating your own cloner effect.\nBefore starting out, make sure you are familiar with the mesh2d workflow and attribute flow.\n\nThe general concept of a cloner is to take the incoming texture and repeat it many times in some sort of pattern. In this patch we'll be doing this by using meshes as meshes are much lighter than using textures. For example: 200 meshes is fine, 200 textures will grind your GPU to a halt."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
