      "3": {
        "attributes": {
          "alignment": {
            "type": "integer",
            "value": 0
          },
          "fill": {
            "type": "bool",
            "value": false
          },
          "font-size": {
            "type": "float",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "MATERIAL\n\nHere we convert our texture into a material to be used in the Mesh2D node."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 291.5706481933594,
          "width": 399.7992858886719,
          "x": 236.80479431152344,
          "y": 1391.0562744140625
        },
        "class": {
          "id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
          "version": 1
        },
        "clock": "video",
        "color": "ffff6a00",
        "constants": {},
        "hidden": [
          "text",
          "alignment",
          "font-size",
          "fill"
        ],
        "name": "Comment",
        "thumbnail_visible": true
      },
      "31": {
        "attributes": {
          "alignment": {
            "type": "integer",
            "value": 0
          },
          "fill": {
            "type": "bool",
            "value": false
          },
          "font-size": {
            "type": "float",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "GEOMETRY AND ASPECT RATIO\n\nHere we create our geometry to project our texture onto.\nFirst we take the aspect ratio of the Patch info node.\nWe unpack this and check whether the resolution's width is greater than its height and allocate the correct rectangle.\n\nThis is to ensure that no matter the aspect ratio of the composition, our rectangle geometry has the right size and orientation."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 525.004150390625,
          "width": 1006.2522583007812,
          "x": -543.0108032226562,
          "y": 26.37969970703125
        },
        "class": {
          "id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
          "version": 1
        },
        "clock": "video",
        "color": "ff02bbff",
        "constants": {},
        "hidden": [
          "text",
          "alignment",
          "font-size",
          "fill"
        ],
        "name": "Comment",
        "thumbnail_visible": true
      },
      "32": {
        "attributes": {
          "alignment": {
            "type": "integer",
            "value": 0
          },
          "fill": {
            "type": "bool",
            "value": false
          },
          "font-size": {
            "type": "float",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "LINEAR TRANSLATION\n\nThis is where the magic happens.\nFirst we have an integer slider at attribute flow to tell the Linear nodes how big they should be.\nWhich in practice translates to how many clones there are, hence the name of the parameter.\n\nThe Width float slider sets how wide the clones should be distributed.\nBy negating the value for the min, we get an even spread for left and right.\n\nThe Distortion float slider sets how much distortion there is on the Y axis.\nWe start with a Linear node producing values from 0 to 1.\nNext, we send it into a curve node which will turn the 0 to 1 range into a \"-Distortion to Distortion\" range with the given curve.\n\nThe two ranges go into a Float2 node, before being sent to the Transformation2D node.\n\nThis is also the part of the patch where all the creative freedom is found.\nYou could try replacing this whol part twith a Circle Pattern or Gradient pattern, or calculate your own."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 807.6675415039062,
          "width": 1183.279296875,
          "x": -546.6154174804688,
          "y": 565.0358276367188
        },
        "class": {
          "id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
          "version": 1
        },
        "clock": "video",
        "color": "ffae7bff",
        "constants": {},
        "hidden": [
          "text",
          "alignment",
          "font-size",
          "fill"
        ],
        "name": "Comment",
        "thumbnail_visible": true
      },
      "33": {
        "attributes": {
          "alignment": {
            "type": "integer",
            "value": 0
          },
          "fill": {
            "type": "bool",
            "value": false
          },
          "font-size": {
            "type": "float",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "RENDERING\n\nThis is the final part of the patch were we create the mesh and render it to a texture."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 411.4664916992187,
          "width": 1200.22998046875,
          "x": 604.6201782226562,
